Subject: [PATCH] ARM: tegra30: microsoft-surface-rt: keep vdd_cover always on

The Type/Touch cover is a HID-over-I2C device behind an i2c-hotplug-gpio
mux. Its supply, the TPS65911 LDO3 rail "vdd_cover", is only referenced
by the cover@0 child node, and that child is only instantiated after the
cover has been detected. Until then nothing holds the regulator, so the
kernel switches the unused rail off at late init. If cover detection needs
the cover to be powered, it can then never happen, and the keyboard stays
dead.

Mark the rail regulator-always-on so it stays powered and the cover is
detected.

Tested on a Microsoft Surface RT booted over APX (Fusee Gelee + U-Boot):
before the change the regulator reported "disabled" and no cover I2C
device appeared; with it, the cover keyboard works.

---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/nvidia/tegra30-microsoft-surface-rt.dts
@@ -317,6 +317,7 @@
 					regulator-name = "vdd_cover";
 					regulator-min-microvolt = <2800000>;
 					regulator-max-microvolt = <2800000>;
+					regulator-always-on;
 					regulator-boot-on;
 				};
 
